1
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:46,900
"The Missing Piece"

2
00:01:47,100 --> 00:01:51,800
(Episode 9)

3
00:02:06,719 --> 00:02:07,840
Why don't I draw Zhou Yang?

4
00:02:28,280 --> 00:02:29,560
Or maybe I'll draw you.

5
00:02:30,159 --> 00:02:31,839
You just love this sofa bed.

6
00:02:31,840 --> 00:02:33,159
You won't even sleep with me.

7
00:03:14,479 --> 00:03:16,080
Your right hand is badly hurt.

8
00:03:16,319 --> 00:03:17,719
There may be lasting effects.

9
00:03:17,879 --> 00:03:19,400
It could affect your daily life.

10
00:03:19,560 --> 00:03:21,000
Please prepare yourself mentally.

11
00:04:22,800 --> 00:04:23,800
What's going on?

12
00:04:24,160 --> 00:04:25,160
What are you doing?

13
00:04:26,399 --> 00:04:26,639
Ah.

14
00:04:27,079 --> 00:04:27,399
I

15
00:04:27,839 --> 00:04:29,120
I'm just cleaning up.

16
00:04:37,240 --> 00:04:38,240
Why are you crying?

17
00:04:42,959 --> 00:04:43,959
Oh.

18
00:04:44,399 --> 00:04:46,279
I probably slept too much this afternoon.

19
00:04:46,959 --> 00:04:47,959
I'm fine.

20
00:04:57,759 --> 00:04:58,759
It hurts.

21
00:05:02,279 --> 00:05:04,399
It's probably just that my
hand hasn't fully healed yet.

22
00:05:04,879 --> 00:05:05,999
Once it heals, I'll be fine.

23
00:05:06,519 --> 00:05:08,279
Even if it never fully heals, it's okay.

24
00:05:09,360 --> 00:05:10,920
Worst case, I just stop drawing.

25
00:05:12,199 --> 00:05:13,599
I'll just get a different job then.

26
00:05:14,040 --> 00:05:16,120
Insurance or sales.

27
00:05:16,959 --> 00:05:18,399
I might even earn more.

28
00:05:19,199 --> 00:05:20,359
You can't hold the brush anymore?

29
00:05:25,839 --> 00:05:26,839
Mm.

30
00:05:48,199 --> 00:05:49,199
I'm here for you.

31
00:05:50,279 --> 00:05:51,279
Mm.

32
00:05:54,240 --> 00:05:55,319
Don't worry.

33
00:05:56,759 --> 00:05:58,240
I'll be fine.

34
00:06:04,040 --> 00:06:06,000
Don't worry.

35
00:06:16,279 --> 00:06:17,279
Come on, Shen Mo.

36
00:06:17,720 --> 00:06:18,720
You can do it.

37
00:06:19,879 --> 00:06:21,560
So I won't be a burden to Yang.

38
00:06:23,399 --> 00:06:24,399
You can do it.

39
00:06:31,600 --> 00:06:32,120
Hello.

40
00:06:32,120 --> 00:06:33,120
And you are?

41
00:06:33,480 --> 00:06:35,878
I'm the one who contacted you online.

42
00:06:35,879 --> 00:06:37,800
Here to apply for the
painting teacher position.

43
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:39,040
Did you bring your resume?

44
00:06:48,120 --> 00:06:49,120
Shen Mo.

45
00:06:49,240 --> 00:06:50,679
Your resume is really impressive.

46
00:06:50,680 --> 00:06:51,680
No, no, not at all.

47
00:06:52,079 --> 00:06:52,639
Ah.

48
00:06:52,640 --> 00:06:54,136
So you've been trained
since childhood, right?

49
00:06:54,160 --> 00:06:55,656
I've been learning to
paint since I was little.

50
00:06:55,680 --> 00:06:57,879
And I kept doing part-time
work through college.

51
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:00,120
So I'm pretty experienced.

52
00:07:00,240 --> 00:07:01,439
Take a look at my paintings.

53
00:07:08,240 --> 00:07:09,240
Oh wow.

54
00:07:09,480 --> 00:07:10,519
This is really well done.

55
00:07:10,839 --> 00:07:11,600
Formally trained.

56
00:07:11,600 --> 00:07:12,560
And you draw this well.

57
00:07:12,560 --> 00:07:13,560
Hey.

58
00:07:13,639 --> 00:07:15,279
What made you think of my little studio?

59
00:07:16,319 --> 00:07:18,480
I haven't worked since I graduated.

60
00:07:18,959 --> 00:07:21,240
My partner's been
supporting me this whole time.

61
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:23,440
He leaves early and comes home late.

62
00:07:24,160 --> 00:07:25,278
It kind of hurts me

63
00:07:25,279 --> 00:07:26,279
I want to...

64
00:07:26,399 --> 00:07:27,519
help share the load.

65
00:07:28,199 --> 00:07:28,839
Mm.

66
00:07:28,839 --> 00:07:29,839
Got it.

67
00:07:29,959 --> 00:07:31,599
But the pay here isn't great.

68
00:07:31,600 --> 00:07:31,959
Ah.

69
00:07:31,960 --> 00:07:33,040
That's fine, that's fine.

70
00:07:33,240 --> 00:07:34,240
In that case.

71
00:07:34,319 --> 00:07:35,839
Just do a quick sketch first.

72
00:07:36,040 --> 00:07:37,560
And I'll take a look at your basic skills.

73
00:07:43,399 --> 00:07:44,000
Uh.

74
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:44,399
What is it?

75
00:07:44,423 --> 00:07:45,423
Is it a bad time?

76
00:07:45,480 --> 00:07:46,480
Well.

77
00:07:47,199 --> 00:07:48,959
I hurt my hand a while back.

78
00:07:49,439 --> 00:07:50,439
Ah.

79
00:07:50,480 --> 00:07:51,079
It's fine.

80
00:07:51,480 --> 00:07:52,639
Just draw something simple

81
00:07:52,759 --> 00:07:54,103
I'll just get the gist.

82
00:07:54,319 --> 00:07:56,040
We only teach little kids here.

83
00:07:56,560 --> 00:07:58,040
As long as you're decent, it's fine.

84
00:08:14,360 --> 00:08:15,000
Hey.

85
00:08:15,001 --> 00:08:16,600
Shen Mo, what are you...?

86
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:21,399
After I hurt my hand.

87
00:08:21,959 --> 00:08:23,040
I can't grip a brush anymore.

88
00:08:24,079 --> 00:08:26,680
You can't even grip it this much?

89
00:08:28,040 --> 00:08:29,439
I've tried so many times.

90
00:08:29,680 --> 00:08:30,680
Not really.

91
00:08:31,639 --> 00:08:32,639
Ah.

92
00:08:32,799 --> 00:08:33,879
How long till it heals?

93
00:08:34,279 --> 00:08:35,279
I don't know either.

94
00:08:35,559 --> 00:08:36,559
Oh boy.

95
00:08:37,559 --> 00:08:38,759
Then there's nothing I can do.

96
00:08:39,440 --> 00:08:41,000
If you can't paint

97
00:08:41,240 --> 00:08:43,240
I can't hire you even if I want to.

98
00:08:43,660 --> 00:08:44,799
Boss, don't worry.

99
00:08:44,840 --> 00:08:46,398
Whether it's skill or ability

100
00:08:46,399 --> 00:08:47,559
I can do it all.

101
00:08:48,080 --> 00:08:49,799
Whether you want me to teach or paint

102
00:08:49,960 --> 00:08:50,999
I can teach anything

103
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:52,320
I can do anything too.

104
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:54,239
I believe in your skill

105
00:08:54,240 --> 00:08:55,839
I believe in your teaching too.

106
00:08:55,840 --> 00:08:57,159
But you can't paint right now.

107
00:08:57,240 --> 00:08:59,200
What about when the kids need a demo piece?

108
00:08:59,440 --> 00:09:00,558
I can't exactly tell the kids

109
00:09:00,559 --> 00:09:01,840
the teacher can't paint.

110
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:03,160
That just doesn't make sense.

111
00:09:05,399 --> 00:09:07,080
I've already sent out so many resumes.

112
00:09:07,440 --> 00:09:08,559
Please, boss

113
00:09:08,720 --> 00:09:09,600
I'm really sorry.

114
00:09:09,720 --> 00:09:10,878
My hands are tied too.

115
00:09:10,879 --> 00:09:11,679
Try your best.

116
00:09:11,680 --> 00:09:13,319
Go get your hand checked first.

117
00:09:13,320 --> 00:09:14,320
How about this?

118
00:09:14,600 --> 00:09:16,639
Once your hand is better, contact me anytime.

119
00:09:19,399 --> 00:09:20,399
Alright.

120
00:09:20,759 --> 00:09:21,759
Thanks, boss.

121
00:09:24,759 --> 00:09:25,759
Ah.

122
00:09:39,626 --> 00:09:44,339
[Desperately searching
for library shelvers]

123
00:10:03,080 --> 00:10:04,080
Shen Mo.

124
00:10:08,600 --> 00:10:09,600
Shen Mo.

125
00:10:23,679 --> 00:10:24,360
Mr. Ji.

126
00:10:24,360 --> 00:10:25,360
Found him.

127
00:10:25,960 --> 00:10:26,960
Good.

128
00:10:34,039 --> 00:10:35,039
Little Shen.

129
00:10:35,440 --> 00:10:36,679
Work faster.

130
00:10:36,919 --> 00:10:38,039
You're so young.

131
00:10:39,840 --> 00:10:40,559
Ah.

132
00:10:40,559 --> 00:10:41,559
Got it, boss.

133
00:11:04,399 --> 00:11:05,399
Shen Mo.

134
00:11:22,519 --> 00:11:23,639
What are you doing here?

135
00:11:26,360 --> 00:11:28,398
I got a job as a library shelver.

136
00:11:28,399 --> 00:11:29,720
Today's my first trial day.

137
00:11:30,200 --> 00:11:31,880
Why didn't you tell me you were going out?

138
00:11:32,399 --> 00:11:33,399
Huh?

139
00:11:34,399 --> 00:11:35,960
Did you think I'd gone missing?

140
00:11:36,279 --> 00:11:37,759
You've been looking for me all along.

141
00:11:39,399 --> 00:11:41,039
You're still not over your illness.

142
00:11:41,679 --> 00:11:43,559
What if you wandered off
and something happened?

143
00:11:44,159 --> 00:11:45,159
Oh, come on.

144
00:11:45,480 --> 00:11:46,639
It's fine.

145
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:48,919
How could I ever bear
to leave you alone?

146
00:11:53,240 --> 00:11:54,559
Why do you want to do this?

147
00:11:56,519 --> 00:11:57,959
I just thought

148
00:11:57,960 --> 00:11:59,759
I could help out with the family bills.

149
00:12:10,639 --> 00:12:11,639
Silly.

150
00:12:12,200 --> 00:12:13,720
We don't need you doing this.

151
00:12:15,440 --> 00:12:16,440
Does this go here?

152
00:12:17,559 --> 00:12:18,039
Ah.

153
00:12:18,039 --> 00:12:19,039
Yeah.

154
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:21,000
These.

155
00:12:21,535 --> 00:12:22,775
These is all my work,

156
00:12:22,799 --> 00:12:23,799
I can handle it myself.

157
00:12:24,759 --> 00:12:26,320
Our boss is watching the whole time.

158
00:12:28,279 --> 00:12:29,279
Let me do it.

159
00:12:29,519 --> 00:12:30,519
Go home and wait for me.

160
00:12:32,200 --> 00:12:32,679
Mm.

161
00:12:32,879 --> 00:12:33,879
Don't worry.

162
00:12:34,399 --> 00:12:35,399
Okay.

163
00:12:55,759 --> 00:12:57,000
You're off work so early today.

164
00:12:59,039 --> 00:13:00,039
How was it?

165
00:13:00,440 --> 00:13:01,600
Was work tiring today?

166
00:13:02,519 --> 00:13:03,519
Not too bad.

167
00:13:06,080 --> 00:13:07,080
Uh.

168
00:13:07,159 --> 00:13:08,919
You don't have to work on weekends, right?

169
00:13:11,120 --> 00:13:11,840
Nope.

170
00:13:11,864 --> 00:13:12,864
What's up?

171
00:13:15,080 --> 00:13:16,560
Wanna go to an art show this weekend?

172
00:13:17,240 --> 00:13:18,960
My friend just gave me two tickets.

173
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:20,000
Whoa.

174
00:13:24,559 --> 00:13:26,039
Did your friend give you the tickets?

175
00:13:26,320 --> 00:13:30,098
Or did you know I wanted to go
and asked a friend for them on purpose?

176
00:13:33,360 --> 00:13:34,800
Just tell me, are you coming or not?

177
00:13:37,279 --> 00:13:38,279
Yes yes yes.

178
00:13:39,039 --> 00:13:40,240
As long as I'm with you.

179
00:13:40,720 --> 00:13:41,720
Anywhere is fine.

180
00:14:13,240 --> 00:14:14,240
Look at this.

181
00:14:15,879 --> 00:14:16,879
Whoa.

182
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:18,560
Seeing those paintings by the masters...

183
00:14:18,919 --> 00:14:20,039
they're really amazing.

184
00:14:21,519 --> 00:14:22,600
I've seen your paintings.

185
00:14:23,639 --> 00:14:24,679
You paint really well too.

186
00:14:25,039 --> 00:14:26,720
How could I compare to them?

187
00:14:28,440 --> 00:14:31,039
Quit your library job.

188
00:14:32,480 --> 00:14:33,480
Why?

189
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:38,463
Have you ever seen a master
who works in a library?

190
00:14:40,720 --> 00:14:42,799
Suffering is the breeding
ground for creativity.

191
00:14:45,639 --> 00:14:47,120
I would never let you suffer.

192
00:14:51,639 --> 00:14:53,159
Once we get your hand fixed

193
00:14:54,200 --> 00:14:55,200
keep painting

194
00:14:55,639 --> 00:14:57,119
until you're better than all of them.

195
00:15:04,080 --> 00:15:06,000
So once I become a great painter

196
00:15:06,272 --> 00:15:07,313
and start making money,

197
00:15:08,399 --> 00:15:10,158
I'll buy you that big
house across the street.

198
00:15:10,159 --> 00:15:11,159
Okay.

199
00:15:12,960 --> 00:15:15,039
Then I'll hold my art show right here

200
00:15:15,519 --> 00:15:17,479
and you just wait for me
at home like a good boy.

201
00:15:19,240 --> 00:15:20,240
Okay.

202
00:15:20,759 --> 00:15:22,199
Then I'll wait for you to come home.

203
00:15:26,960 --> 00:15:28,758
All contract documents in this batch

204
00:15:28,759 --> 00:15:31,240
strictly follow the group's
three-tier review process.

205
00:15:31,360 --> 00:15:33,399
First, the department
head does the initial review,

206
00:15:33,879 --> 00:15:35,799
checking the data
and the plan's feasibility.

207
00:15:36,080 --> 00:15:38,279
Then the deputy GM reviews and confirms

208
00:15:38,639 --> 00:15:40,480
to control project and funding risks.

209
00:15:41,200 --> 00:15:42,200
Finally, Legal

210
00:15:42,279 --> 00:15:44,559
and Risk Control do a
double compliance check

211
00:15:45,120 --> 00:15:46,120
to verify...

212
00:15:48,440 --> 00:15:49,440
Mr. Ji.

213
00:15:49,840 --> 00:15:53,159
Is something wrong with my plan?

214
00:15:55,279 --> 00:15:56,279
No, no.

215
00:15:56,399 --> 00:15:57,840
Just go with your plan.

216
00:15:57,919 --> 00:15:58,919
Meeting adjourned.

217
00:16:03,320 --> 00:16:03,960
Mr. Ji

218
00:16:03,961 --> 00:16:05,521
I was just about to get your signature.

219
00:16:05,759 --> 00:16:06,559
No time.

220
00:16:06,600 --> 00:16:07,399
Some other day

221
00:16:07,600 --> 00:16:08,640
I'm going to the hospital.

222
00:16:09,159 --> 00:16:10,519
Huh? What are you sick with?

223
00:16:11,200 --> 00:16:12,200
I'm not sick

224
00:16:12,399 --> 00:16:13,399
I'm visiting a patient.

225
00:16:24,720 --> 00:16:26,320
I've never seen Mr. Ji like this.

226
00:16:26,679 --> 00:16:27,679
Yeah.

227
00:16:28,480 --> 00:16:29,840
Feels like he's in love.

228
00:16:30,879 --> 00:16:32,320
Don't worry about that.

229
00:16:33,080 --> 00:16:35,360
I got you the best
hospital and specialists here.

230
00:16:35,960 --> 00:16:37,320
This hand repair surgery of yours...

231
00:16:37,879 --> 00:16:38,879
It'll be fine for sure.

232
00:16:46,960 --> 00:16:47,960
Mm.

233
00:16:54,919 --> 00:16:56,759
What if it can't be cured?

234
00:16:58,679 --> 00:16:59,959
What if the surgery fails?

235
00:16:59,960 --> 00:17:01,360
What if it gets worse?

236
00:17:02,320 --> 00:17:03,320
Don't be scared.

237
00:17:03,600 --> 00:17:04,759
It'll be fine for sure.

238
00:17:05,960 --> 00:17:07,200
No matter what happens.

239
00:17:08,319 --> 00:17:09,599
I'll be right by your side.

240
00:17:14,720 --> 00:17:15,759
I lied.

241
00:17:15,839 --> 00:17:16,920
I'm not scared at all.

242
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:19,480
If it works, great.

243
00:17:19,839 --> 00:17:21,319
If it fails, no regrets.

244
00:17:22,759 --> 00:17:23,759
Besides.

245
00:17:24,039 --> 00:17:25,359
As long as you're by my side

246
00:17:25,559 --> 00:17:26,680
I'm not afraid of anything.

247
00:17:28,440 --> 00:17:30,518
Sometimes I really can't figure you out.

248
00:17:30,542 --> 00:17:31,542
Mm?

249
00:17:33,400 --> 00:17:35,440
So soft-tempered, like
anyone can push you around.

250
00:17:37,079 --> 00:17:38,319
But once you dig in your heels.

251
00:17:39,599 --> 00:17:40,799
You're stubborn as hell.

252
00:17:43,200 --> 00:17:45,079
Is that a compliment or an insult?

253
00:17:47,559 --> 00:17:48,400
Guess.

254
00:17:48,400 --> 00:17:49,200
Alright.

255
00:17:49,201 --> 00:17:50,480
Don't be so nervous.

256
00:17:51,359 --> 00:17:53,920
By this time tomorrow,
the surgery will be over.

257
00:17:55,119 --> 00:17:56,119
It's nothing.

258
00:17:57,960 --> 00:17:59,880
I just don't like hospitals much.

259
00:18:01,720 --> 00:18:02,720
My mother...

260
00:18:03,319 --> 00:18:04,319
Mm?

261
00:18:05,680 --> 00:18:07,000
Let's talk about that later.

262
00:18:08,119 --> 00:18:09,680
You should get some rest today.

263
00:18:11,160 --> 00:18:12,480
The surgery is tomorrow.

264
00:18:19,619 --> 00:18:21,246
[Operation on-going]

265
00:18:49,200 --> 00:18:50,000
Doctor.

266
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:50,759
How was it?

267
00:18:50,832 --> 00:18:51,913
Was the surgery successful?

268
00:18:52,732 --> 00:18:53,732
Very successful.

269
00:19:01,440 --> 00:19:02,440
Hang in there.

270
00:19:07,200 --> 00:19:08,200
The surgery went great.

271
00:19:09,759 --> 00:19:11,240
You'll be out of here soon.

272
00:19:13,039 --> 00:19:14,960
Before the anesthesia, I'd already decided.

273
00:19:15,680 --> 00:19:17,319
If the surgery failed,

274
00:19:18,079 --> 00:19:20,359
worst case, you can be my right hand.

275
00:19:20,480 --> 00:19:21,480
Don't talk nonsense.

276
00:19:22,640 --> 00:19:23,720
Once you're discharged,

277
00:19:24,960 --> 00:19:26,640
I'll take you out for something good.

278
00:19:27,160 --> 00:19:28,160
Okay.

279
00:19:28,519 --> 00:19:29,200
Wow.

280
00:19:29,200 --> 00:19:30,200
So much food.

281
00:19:30,359 --> 00:19:31,759
It all looks so delicious.

282
00:19:32,400 --> 00:19:32,920
Of course.

283
00:19:33,240 --> 00:19:34,680
This is my secret spot.

284
00:19:35,119 --> 00:19:35,839
I usually

285
00:19:35,840 --> 00:19:37,000
don't bring just anyone here.

286
00:19:38,359 --> 00:19:39,559
Such a great place.

287
00:19:39,960 --> 00:19:41,480
Who have you been bringing here?

288
00:19:41,880 --> 00:19:42,480
Yang.

289
00:19:42,480 --> 00:19:43,119
Yang.

290
00:19:43,120 --> 00:19:44,279
You'd better come clean.

291
00:19:45,480 --> 00:19:46,680
Let me run something by you.

292
00:19:48,240 --> 00:19:49,839
Starting today, you're living with me

293
00:19:50,119 --> 00:19:51,159
I already found the place.

294
00:19:51,160 --> 00:19:52,160
Why?

295
00:19:52,459 --> 00:19:54,499
Isn't our place now pretty good?

296
00:19:55,400 --> 00:19:57,160
You'll like our new home even more.

297
00:20:11,119 --> 00:20:12,759
So where exactly is our new home?

298
00:20:23,940 --> 00:20:24,940
This...

299
00:20:25,360 --> 00:20:26,360
Isn't this...

300
00:20:26,640 --> 00:20:27,640
Yep.

301
00:20:28,039 --> 00:20:30,440
So you can become a great painter sooner.

302
00:20:31,920 --> 00:20:33,880
Of course we should live near the gallery.

303
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:36,000
But.

304
00:20:36,680 --> 00:20:38,079
This must cost a fortune.

305
00:20:38,119 --> 00:20:39,240
Such a nice neighborhood.

306
00:20:39,960 --> 00:20:43,599
And didn't you say back then
that you were giving it to me?

307
00:20:44,720 --> 00:20:46,000
This is an investment.

308
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:48,599
You're a future great painter.

309
00:20:51,640 --> 00:20:52,640
Okay.

310
00:20:52,799 --> 00:20:54,519
Then I, the great painter Shen.

311
00:20:54,920 --> 00:20:56,200
For my comeback piece

312
00:20:56,559 --> 00:20:58,480
I'll paint you first, okay.

313
00:20:59,880 --> 00:21:01,160
Or maybe a Ferris wheel.

314
00:21:01,680 --> 00:21:02,680
Ferris wheel?

315
00:21:05,359 --> 00:21:06,359
Yeah.

316
00:21:06,880 --> 00:21:08,359
Near your old rental place.

317
00:21:08,480 --> 00:21:09,960
Isn't there a big Ferris wheel?

318
00:21:11,400 --> 00:21:13,880
I won you over right
under that Ferris wheel.

319
00:21:31,359 --> 00:21:32,359
Don't move.

320
00:21:33,160 --> 00:21:34,240
Your hand's not healed yet.

321
00:21:38,440 --> 00:21:39,440
Thanks for your effort.

322
00:21:44,359 --> 00:21:45,599
Did you forget something?

323
00:21:47,480 --> 00:21:48,480
Hmm?

324
00:21:49,839 --> 00:21:50,839
Give me your hand.

325
00:22:17,759 --> 00:22:18,759
Yang.

326
00:22:20,279 --> 00:22:22,319
Do you think my hand can still heal?

327
00:22:23,839 --> 00:22:24,839
Of course.

328
00:22:25,839 --> 00:22:27,000
As long as you keep at it.

329
00:22:28,559 --> 00:22:29,960
It'll pay off for sure.

330
00:22:32,160 --> 00:22:33,160
It definitely will.

331
00:22:35,839 --> 00:22:36,839
Okay.

332
00:22:37,633 --> 00:22:39,312
Then once my hand heals,

333
00:22:40,079 --> 00:22:42,960
I want to turn that empty south-facing room

334
00:22:43,200 --> 00:22:44,240
into a studio.

335
00:22:44,440 --> 00:22:47,359
And fill it with all my paintings.

336
00:22:48,640 --> 00:22:51,360
By then, that one of
the Ferris wheel will go right in the center.

337
00:22:51,519 --> 00:22:52,920
So you'll see it right away.

338
00:22:57,519 --> 00:22:58,519
Okay.

339
00:22:59,759 --> 00:23:00,759
Mm.

340
00:23:01,640 --> 00:23:03,920
Then I'll just paint at home.

341
00:23:04,839 --> 00:23:06,480
Cook for you at home.

342
00:23:06,960 --> 00:23:09,480
And sing for you too.

343
00:23:10,599 --> 00:23:13,279
We'll plan where to travel together.

344
00:23:14,920 --> 00:23:16,559
Sounds good.

345
00:25:00,119 --> 00:25:01,920
I've got to find a chance to devour you.

346
00:25:06,799 --> 00:25:07,799
Merry Christmas.

347
00:25:10,319 --> 00:25:11,440
During the New Year,

348
00:25:11,960 --> 00:25:13,680
I'm planning to go abroad to see my family.

349
00:25:15,000 --> 00:25:15,400
Okay.

350
00:25:15,400 --> 00:25:16,400
Alright.

351
00:25:16,440 --> 00:25:18,200
Then I'll just wait for you to come back.

352
00:25:20,519 --> 00:25:21,519
What about you?

353
00:25:21,966 --> 00:25:26,626
Are you home alone or going back
to your hometown for New Year's?

354
00:25:27,839 --> 00:25:28,519
It's fine

355
00:25:28,520 --> 00:25:29,840
I'll just go back to my hometown.

356
00:25:30,119 --> 00:25:31,240
Don't worry about me.

357
00:25:44,119 --> 00:25:45,240
Merry Christmas.

358
00:26:31,559 --> 00:26:32,920
I miss you.

359
00:26:36,440 --> 00:26:37,440
Stop it.

360
00:27:36,400 --> 00:27:37,400
Yang.

361
00:27:51,359 --> 00:27:52,440
I'm not Zhou Yang.

362
00:27:58,373 --> 00:27:59,893
You're the one I love the most.

363
00:28:01,886 --> 00:28:03,045
How could I be wrong?

364
00:28:14,279 --> 00:28:15,519
You're still not well.

365
00:28:17,720 --> 00:28:19,240
I was never sick.

366
00:28:41,039 --> 00:28:42,599
We'll continue when you're better.

367
00:29:07,000 --> 00:29:08,000
Hey.

368
00:29:08,480 --> 00:29:09,480
What are you up to?

369
00:29:10,032 --> 00:29:11,072
I'm alone...

370
00:29:12,680 --> 00:29:14,359
I'm home cleaning.

371
00:29:14,799 --> 00:29:16,200
Weren't you going back home?

372
00:29:16,960 --> 00:29:17,720
It's close

373
00:29:17,920 --> 00:29:19,200
I'll leave once I'm done.

374
00:29:19,559 --> 00:29:20,000
Ugh.

375
00:29:20,001 --> 00:29:21,720
Yang, don't worry about me.

376
00:29:21,960 --> 00:29:23,640
Just stay abroad with your family.

377
00:29:24,960 --> 00:29:25,960
Mm.

378
00:29:26,839 --> 00:29:28,359
Remember to put medicine on your hand.

379
00:29:29,960 --> 00:29:31,119
Don't worry.

380
00:29:31,559 --> 00:29:32,079
Okay

381
00:29:32,079 --> 00:29:33,079
I'm hanging up then.

382
00:29:39,799 --> 00:29:40,960
Almost blew it.

383
00:29:56,920 --> 00:29:57,920
Are you asleep?

384
00:30:00,720 --> 00:30:01,799
Not asleep yet.

385
00:30:02,160 --> 00:30:03,240
Waiting for midnight.

386
00:30:04,319 --> 00:30:05,319
You?

387
00:30:05,359 --> 00:30:06,400
Still having dinner.

388
00:30:09,200 --> 00:30:10,200
Oh right.

389
00:30:11,160 --> 00:30:12,360
We're in different time zones.

390
00:30:13,960 --> 00:30:15,440
Is it fun spending New Year abroad?

391
00:30:16,400 --> 00:30:17,400
Nothing special.

392
00:30:18,079 --> 00:30:19,079
Mo.

393
00:30:19,480 --> 00:30:20,480
Where are you now?

394
00:30:22,319 --> 00:30:23,400
I'm home.

395
00:30:25,440 --> 00:30:26,440
Alone?

396
00:30:30,240 --> 00:30:31,320
I went back to my hometown.

397
00:30:31,720 --> 00:30:32,839
My parents are both here.

398
00:30:35,359 --> 00:30:36,359
Mo.

399
00:30:38,799 --> 00:30:39,799
Happy New Year.

400
00:30:43,559 --> 00:30:44,640
Happy New Year.

401
00:31:01,079 --> 00:31:02,079
Yang.

402
00:31:02,319 --> 00:31:04,240
What are you doing right now?
